//################################ pinktrombone.lib ##########################################
// A Faust port of Neil Thapen's **Pink Trombone** (2017), the bare-handed procedural
// speech synthesiser <https://dood.al/pinktrombone/>.
//
// The original is a ~1000-line JavaScript program running in a ScriptProcessorNode.
// This library reproduces its DSP core:
//
// * **Glottis** — a per-period-resampled Liljencrants–Fant (LF) glottal-flow
//   waveform driven by a single "tenseness" parameter (Rd = 3(1-tenseness)),
//   plus aspiration noise modulated by the glottal cycle, vibrato / pitch wobble
//   and slow tenseness drift.
// * **Tract** — a 44-section Kelly–Lochbaum digital waveguide of the vocal
//   tract, run at *twice* the audio rate (two waveguide ticks per sample),
//   with a 28-section nasal branch coupled at section 17 by a three-port
//   scattering junction, glottal reflection 0.75, lip/nostril reflection -0.85,
//   fricative turbulence injected at a movable constriction, and a decaying
//   "transient" pulse released when a full closure opens (plosives).
// * **Tract shape** — the "tongue" (index / diameter) that bends the rest
//   diameters between the blade and the lips, one or two constrictions
//   (index / diameter, e.g. for fricatives and stops), and the velum.
//
// Everything that was block-rate (512 samples) in the JavaScript is computed
// at sample rate here, with the block-rate constants converted to rates using
// the original's block length.
//
// **Sample rate.** Each waveguide section is one tick long, so the tract's
// acoustic length, and with it every formant, scales with the tick rate; the
// original has the same property. With the default `ticksPerSample = 2` the
// model is tuned for 44.1 and 48 kHz (at 48 kHz the formants of a given shape
// are about 9 % higher than at 44.1 kHz). At 88.2 or 96 kHz, override it to 1,
// e.g. `pt[ticksPerSample=1;].pinkTrombone(...)`: the whole model then behaves
// as it does at 44.1 or 48 kHz. Other rates shift the formants in proportion.
// The 1-D simplex drift noises are the real thing (`no.simplex1_lf`, a port of
// the same noisejs code, with a fixed seed instead of `Date.now()`); the browser's
// uniform `Math.random()` white noise is replaced by scaled `no.noise`.
//
// Its official prefix is `pt`.
//
// #### Deviations from the original
//
// * The block-rate updates (512-sample blocks) run at sample rate, and the reflection
//   coefficients follow the section diameters every sample instead of being
//   interpolated across each block (which also removes the original's swapped
//   old/new interpolation at the nose junction). The release of a closure is still
//   detected one block late, as in the original.
// * `voiced` behaves like a finger on the original's pitch keyboard: voicing ramps
//   in and out, without the pressed onset of the original's untouched "always
//   voice" start-up.
// * UI-only behaviour is not modelled: the keyboard is replaced by `freq` in Hz;
//   the tongue control's reachable-range kludge, and its side effect of acting as a
//   wide constriction while held, are left out; at most two constrictions
//   (`tract2`, `pinkTrombone2`); the velum is the separate `nasal` gate instead of a
//   touch below the tract.
// * Up to two release transients sound at once (the original keeps a list).
// * The simplex drift uses the fixed seed `noiseSeed` instead of `Date.now()`, and
//   the uniform white noise is scaled `no.noise`.
// * Waveguide state below 1e-20 is flushed to zero, so the (lossless) nose does not
//   decay into denormals.
//
// Against a line-by-line reference port of the JavaScript, settled tract output
// matches to about 1e-6 (relative) and the LF waveform to 2e-3 (absolute, float32).
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// pt = library("pinktrombone.lib");
// process = pt.pinkTrombone(freq, tenseness, voiced, wobble, tongueIndex, tongueDiameter,
//                           constrictionIndex, constrictionDiameter, constrictionOn, nasal);
// ```
//
// Use `process = dm.pink_trombone_demo;` with `import("stdfaust.lib");` for the demo.
//
// Note: pass *signals* (or use partial application / sequential composition) for the
// audio-rate arguments `glottalOutput`, `noiseModulator`, `fricNoise` — an explicit
// `_` argument gets duplicated wherever the parameter is used inside the function.
//
// #### References
//
// * Neil Thapen, *Pink Trombone — bare-handed procedural speech synthesis*,
//   version 1.1 (March 2017), MIT licence. <https://dood.al/pinktrombone/>
// * The original's bibliography: J. O. Smith III, *Physical Audio Signal Processing*
//   <https://ccrma.stanford.edu/~jos/pasp/>; B. H. Story, "A parametric model of the
//   vocal tract area function for vowel and consonant simulation", JASA 117(5), 2005;
//   H.-L. Lu & J. O. Smith, "Glottal source modeling for singing voice synthesis",
//   ICMC 2000; J. Mullen, *Physical modelling of the vocal tract with the 2D digital
//   waveguide mesh*, PhD thesis, York, 2006.
// * G. Fant, "The LF-model revisited. Transformations and frequency domain analysis",
//   STL-QPSR 36(2-3), 1995 (the Rd parametrisation used by `setupWaveform`).
//
// #### License
//
// The Faust port is MIT-licensed, Copyright 2026 David Braun. It is a derivative
// work of *Pink Trombone* version 1.1 (March 2017) by Neil Thapen
// <https://venuspatrol.nfshost.com>; the original copyright and permission notice
// follows, reproduced verbatim as it requires:
//
// Copyright 2017 Neil Thapen
//
// Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a
// copy of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"),
// to deal in the Software without restriction, including without limitation
// the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense,
// and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the
// Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:
//
// The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in
// all copies or substantial portions of the Software.
//
// THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
// IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
// FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
// AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
// LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING
// FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS
// IN THE SOFTWARE.
//########################################################################################

declare name "pinktrombone.lib";
declare version "1.0.0";
declare author "David Braun (Faust port), Neil Thapen (original algorithm)";
declare license "MIT";

aa = library("aanl.lib");
ba = library("basics.lib");
fi = library("filters.lib");
ma = library("maths.lib");
no = library("noises.lib");
os = library("oscillators.lib");
si = library("signals.lib");

//=========================== Constants ================================================
//======================================================================================

_n = 44;                 // number of tract sections
_bladeStart = 10;
_tipStart = 32;
_lipStart = 39;
_noseLength = 28;
_noseStart = _n - _noseLength + 1;   // 17
_glottalReflection = 0.75;
_lipReflection = -0.85;
_movementSpeed = 15;     // "cm per second"
_tractDamping = 0.999;   // per-tick loss in the mouth
_noseDamping = 1.0;      // `fade` in the original (nose has no loss)

//------------------------`(pt.)ticksPerSample`----------------------------------------
// Waveguide ticks per sample (2). The tract's length, and so its formants, follow
// the tick rate: keep 2 at 44.1/48 kHz, override it to 1 at 88.2/96 kHz with
// explicit substitution (`pt[ticksPerSample=1;]`).
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// ticksPerSample : _
// ```
//
// #### Test
// ```
// import("stdfaust.lib");
// pt_ticksPerSample_test = pt[ticksPerSample=1;].pinkTrombone(140, 0.6, 1, 0, 12.9, 2.43, 30, 3, 0, 0);
// ```
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
declare ticksPerSample license "MIT";
ticksPerSample = 2;

// The sample rate at which the original would run the same tract: all its
// block-rate constants refer to 512-sample blocks at that rate.
_equivSR = ma.SR*ticksPerSample/2;
_blockTime = 512.0/_equivSR;

//=========================== Utilities =================================================
//======================================================================================

// Asymmetric slew limiter (rates in units/second). y(0) = x(0): the state is
// the deviation from the target so the smoother starts *on* its target
// instead of at 0 (avoids a spurious "opening" of the tract at start-up).
// A constant input therefore gives a constant output, with no ramp at any
// point — which is what makes a frozen articulation exactly LTI (see `tractExt`).
_moveTowards(up, dn, x) = x - e
with {
    dx = (x - x') * (1');                // 0 on the first sample only
    e = (\(ep).(ep + dx - aa.clip(0 - dn/ma.SR, up/ma.SR, ep + dx))) ~ _;
};

// Latch `x` when `w` is nonzero (also on the very first sample so the _latch
// never sits at an unrelated 0).
_latch(w, x) = x : ba.sAndH(w | (1 - 1'));

// The original's 1-D simplex noise `noise.simplex1(t*rate)`: one seeded permutation
// table shared by all the drift streams (as in the JavaScript, where a single
// `noise` object is evaluated at different rates). Real simplex noise lives in
// `no.simplex1_lf` (noises.lib); `noiseSeed` selects the table (the original
// seeds it from `Date.now()`, i.e. randomly per page load).
//------------------------`(pt.)noiseSeed`----------------------------------------
// Constant integer seed (12345) shared by the simplex drift streams. Override with explicit library substitution to choose another seed.
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// noiseSeed : _
// ```
//
// #### Test
// ```
// import("stdfaust.lib");
// pt_noiseSeed_test = pt[noiseSeed=7;].glottis(140, 0.6, 1, 1) : _, !, !, !;
// ```
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
declare noiseSeed license "MIT";
noiseSeed = 12345;

// Seeded slow simplex drift shared by the modulators.
_simplexNoise(rate) = no.simplex1_lf(noiseSeed, rate);
_simplexNoise(rate) = no.simplex1_lf(noiseSeed, rate);

// The browser fed one uniform [0,1) white noise into two bandpass filters
// (BiquadFilterNode "bandpass", unity peak). Faust `no.noise` is [-1,1], so
// halve it; the DC offset is removed by the bandpass anyway.
_whiteNoise = 0.5*no.noise;
_bandpassUnity(fc, Q) = fi.resonbp(fc, Q, 1/Q);
_aspirationNoise = _whiteNoise : _bandpassUnity(500, 0.5);
_fricativeNoise = _whiteNoise : _bandpassUnity(1000, 0.5);

//=========================== Glottis ===================================================
//======================================================================================

//------------------------`(pt.)lfWaveform`----------------------------------------
// The original's `setupWaveform` + `normalizedLFWaveform`: a Liljencrants–Fant
// glottal flow derivative pulse parametrised by Rd (0.5..2.7), normalised to a
// period of 1 and Ee = 1, evaluated at phase `t` in [0,1).
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// lfWaveform(Rd0, t) : _
// ```
//
// Where:
//
// * `Rd0`: LF shape parameter, clamped to 0.5..2.7.
// * `t`: Phase in the half-open interval [0, 1).
//
// #### Test
// ```
// import("stdfaust.lib");
// lfWaveform_test = par(i, 3, pt.lfWaveform(0.5 + i, os.lf_sawpos(100)));
// lfWaveform_modulated_test = pt.lfWaveform(0.5 + 1.1*(1 + os.osc(2)), os.lf_sawpos(200));
// ```
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
declare lfWaveform license "MIT";
lfWaveform(Rd0, t) = (Rd0 : _lfCoefficients), t : _lfEvaluate;

// Separate shape-dependent setup from phase-dependent evaluation so the
// glottis can hold coefficients for a whole period. The public lfWaveform
// still accepts an audio-rate Rd. Outputs: epsilon, shift, Delta, Te, omega,
// alpha, E0. Keep shared intermediates on wires to bound the block diagram.
_lfCoefficients = shapeRatios : phaseTiming : returnCoefficients : openingCoefficients
with {
    // Rd -> Ra (return duration ratio), Rk (opening ratio), Rg (frequency ratio).
    shapeRatios = aa.clip(0.5, 2.7)
           : \(Rd).(-0.01 + 0.048*Rd, 0.224 + 0.118*Rd, Rd)
           : \(Ra, Rk, Rd).(Ra, Rk, (Rk/4)*(0.5 + 1.2*Rk)/(0.11*Rd - Ra*(0.5 + 1.2*Rk)));

    // Ratios -> Ta (return time), Tp (peak time), Te (end of opening phase).
    phaseTiming = \(Ra, Rk, Rg).(Ra, 1/(2*Rg), Rk)
           : \(Ta, Tp, Rk).(Ta, Tp, Tp + Tp*Rk);

    // Return-phase decay and normalization; carry Tp and Te into the next stage.
    returnCoefficients = \(Ta, Tp, Te).(1/Ta, Tp, Te)
           : \(epsilon, Tp, Te).(epsilon, exp(0 - epsilon*(1 - Te)), Tp, Te)
           : \(epsilon, shift, Tp, Te).(epsilon, shift, 1 - shift, Tp, Te);

    // Balance the opening and return phases for a zero waveform integral.
    openingCoefficients = \(epsilon, shift, Delta, Tp, Te).
                 (epsilon, shift, Delta, Tp, Te, ma.PI/Tp,
                  ((1/epsilon)*(shift - 1) + (1 - Te)*shift)/Delta)
           : \(epsilon, shift, Delta, Tp, Te, omega, RHSIntegral).
                 (epsilon, shift, Delta, Te, omega, sin(omega*Te), Tp,
                  0 - (RHSIntegral - (Te - Tp)/2))
           : \(epsilon, shift, Delta, Te, omega, s, Tp, totalUpperIntegral).
                 (epsilon, shift, Delta, Te, omega, s,
                  log(0 - ma.PI*s*totalUpperIntegral/(Tp*2))/(Tp/2 - Te))
           : \(epsilon, shift, Delta, Te, omega, s, alpha).
                 (epsilon, shift, Delta, Te, omega, alpha, -1.0/(s*exp(alpha*Te)));
};

// Evaluate one phase using the seven shape coefficients above.
_lfEvaluate = \(epsilon, shift, Delta, Te, omega, alpha, E0, t).
    (select2(t > Te,
             E0*exp(alpha*t)*sin(omega*t),
             (shift - exp(0 - epsilon*(t - Te)))/Delta));

//------------------------`(pt.)glottis`----------------------------------------
// The Pink Trombone glottal source. Returns the glottal flow (LF pulse plus
// aspiration noise) that feeds the tract, together with the signals the tract
// needs from the glottis (noise modulator, and glottal-phase & intensity for
// convenience).
// Outputs are glottal excitation, noise modulator, intensity and phase, in that order.
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// glottis(freq, tenseness, voiced, wobble) : _, _, _, _
// ```
//
// Where:
//
// * `freq`: Positive fundamental frequency in Hz; the demo spans about 87..277 Hz.
// * `tenseness`: Voice tenseness in 0..1; the default is 0.6.
// * `voiced`: Voice gate: positive is on, zero is off. It acts like a finger on the
//   original's pitch keyboard: voicing ramps in and out, with no pressed onset.
// * `wobble`: Pitch wobble amount in 0..1.
//
// #### Test
// ```
// import("stdfaust.lib");
// glottis_test = pt.glottis(140, 0.6, (ba.time < 24000), 0);
// glottis_modulated_test = pt.glottis(150 + 50*os.osc(0.8), 0.5 + 0.45*os.osc(4), (ba.time % 48000) > 12000, 1);
// ```
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
declare glottis license "MIT";
glottis(freq, tenseness, voiced, wobble) = voiceIntensity : modulateControls : advancePhase : renderExcitation
with {
    // The stages pass shared signals along as *wires* (sequential composition)
    // instead of referencing `with`-definitions from several places: Faust
    // substitutes definitions textually, so a twice-referenced definition
    // becomes two full subgraphs in the block diagram (the signal compiler
    // CSEs them, the SVG drawer does not).

    // ---- voiceIntensity: intensity (block-rate state of the original, at sample rate)
    // intensity += 0.13 per block when voiced, -= 0.05 per block otherwise, clamped 0..1
    voiceIntensity = _moveTowards(0.13/_blockTime, 0.05/_blockTime, (voiced > 0)) : aa.clip(0, 1);

    // ---- modulateControls: (intensity) -> (intensity, newFrequency, newTenseness) ----
    modulateControls = \(intensity).(intensity, newFrequency(intensity), newTenseness(intensity));

    // smoothFrequency moves by a factor 1.1 per block towards the UI frequency,
    // and snaps to it when intensity == 0.
    newFrequency(intensity) = smoothFrequency*(1 + vibrato)
    with {
        logRate = log(1.1)/_blockTime;
        smoothFrequency = exp(smoothLogFrequency)
        with {
            targetLogFrequency = log(max(1, freq));
            smoothLogFrequency = (\(previous).(select2((intensity == 0) | (1 - 1'),
                                previous + aa.clip(0 - logRate/ma.SR, logRate/ma.SR, targetLogFrequency - previous),
                                targetLogFrequency))) ~ _ ;
        };
        vibrato = 0.005*os.osc(6)
                + 0.02*_simplexNoise(4.07)
                + 0.04*_simplexNoise(2.15)
                + wobble*(0.2*_simplexNoise(0.98) + 0.4*_simplexNoise(0.5));
    };

    // newTenseness: UI tenseness + slow drift. The gate acts like a finger on
    // the original's keyboard, so its untouched "always voice" pressed onset
    // term (3-tenseness)*(1-intensity) does not apply.
    newTenseness(intensity) = tenseness + 0.1*_simplexNoise(0.46) + 0.05*_simplexNoise(0.36);

    // ---- advancePhase: (intensity, newFrequency, newTenseness) -> (intensity, newTenseness, phase, wrap)
    // per-period phasor: the frequency is sampled at the start of each glottal
    // cycle (setupWaveform); wrap is 1 on the sample where a new period starts
    advancePhase = \(intensity, frequency, tenseness).(intensity, tenseness, phaseAndWrap(frequency));
    phaseAndWrap(newFrequency) = (tick ~ (_,_)) : (_,!,_)
    with {
        tick(phase, latchedFrequency) = nextPhase - wrap, select2(wrap, frequency, newFrequency), wrap
        with {
            frequency = select2(latchedFrequency > 0, newFrequency, latchedFrequency);  // first sample: no latched value yet
            nextPhase = phase + frequency/ma.SR;
            wrap = nextPhase >= 1;
        };
    };

    // ---- renderExcitation: (intensity, newTenseness, phase, wrap) -> the four outputs ----
    renderExcitation(intensity, newTenseness, phase, wrap) = glottalOutput, noiseModulator, intensity, phase
    with {
        loudness = pow(tenseness, 0.25);
        // tenseness is sampled at the start of each glottal cycle too
        Rd = 3*(1 - _latch(wrap, newTenseness));
        // Hold the derived coefficients on the same samples as Rd, including
        // sample zero. This reuses them between wraps without control/enable,
        // preserving compatibility with the vector compiler.
        coefficients = Rd : _lfCoefficients : par(i, 7, _latch(wrap));
        voice = (coefficients, phase : _lfEvaluate)*intensity*loudness;

        voicedMod = 0.1 + 0.2*max(0, sin(2*ma.PI*phase));
        noiseModulator = tenseness*intensity*voicedMod + (1 - tenseness*intensity)*0.3;
        aspiration = intensity*(1 - sqrt(tenseness))*noiseModulator*_aspirationNoise
                   * (0.2 + 0.02*_simplexNoise(1.99));

        glottalOutput = voice + aspiration;
    };
};

//=========================== Tract shape ==============================================
//======================================================================================

// Rest diameter of section i given the tongue position (TractUI.setRestDiameter
// plus Tract.init for the sections outside the tongue range).
_restDiameter(tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, i) = ba.if(i < _bladeStart, initial(i),
                                               ba.if(i < _lipStart, tongue, 1.5))
with {
    initial(j) = ba.if(j < 7*_n/44 - 0.5, 0.6, ba.if(j < 12*_n/44, 1.1, 1.5));
    t = 1.1*ma.PI*(tongueIndex - i)/(_tipStart - _bladeStart);
    fixedTongueDiameter = 2 + (tongueDiameter - 2)/1.5;
    edge = ba.if((i == _bladeStart-2) | (i == _lipStart-1), 0.8,
           ba.if((i == _bladeStart) | (i == _lipStart-2), 0.94, 1.0));
    curve = (1.5 - fixedTongueDiameter + 1.7)*cos(t)*edge;   // 1.7 = gridOffset
    tongue = 1.5 - curve;
};

// Target diameter of section i after applying a constriction at fractional
// `index` with (touch-space) `diameter` (TractUI.handleTouches).
_constrictedDiameter(index, diameter, active, i, rest) =
    select2(active & (index >= 2) & (index < _n) & (diameter < 3) & (d < rest),
            rest,
            d + (rest - d)*shrink)
with {
    d = max(0, diameter - 0.3);
    width = ba.if(index < 25, 10,
            ba.if(index >= _tipStart, 5, 10 - 5*(index - 25)/(_tipStart - 25)));
    relpos = abs(i - index) - 0.5;
    shrink = ba.if(relpos <= 0, 0, ba.if(relpos > width, 1, 0.5*(1 - cos(ma.PI*relpos/width))));
};

// Slew rate ("_slowReturn") for section i: the tract re-opens more slowly
// towards the back.
_slowReturn(i) = ba.if(i < _noseStart, 0.6,
                ba.if(i >= _tipStart, 1.0, 0.6 + 0.4*(i - _noseStart)/(_tipStart - _noseStart)));

//------------------------`(pt.)tractDiameters`----------------------------------------
// The 44 time-varying section diameters (after the original's movement
// smoothing), as parallel signals.
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// tractDiameters(tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, cIndex, cDiameter, cActive) : si.bus(44)
// ```
//
// Where:
//
// * `tongueIndex`: Tongue position in sections, 12..29 (default 12.9).
// * `tongueDiameter`: Tongue diameter in model units, 2.05..3.5 (default 2.43).
// * `cIndex`: Constriction position in sections, 2..44; position 44 lies beyond the mouth cells.
// * `cDiameter`: Touch diameter in model units, 0..3; at most 0.3 closes the tract, 3 leaves it open.
// * `cActive`: Constriction gate, 0 or 1.
//
// #### Test
// ```
// import("stdfaust.lib");
// tractDiameters_test = pt.tractDiameters(12.9, 2.43, 30, 3, 0);
// tractDiameters_constricted_test = pt.tractDiameters(20, 3.0, 30.4, 0.55, 1);
// ```
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
declare tractDiameters license "MIT";
tractDiameters(tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, cIndex, cDiameter, cActive) =
    tractDiameters2(tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, cIndex, cDiameter, cActive, 30, 3, 0);

//------------------------`(pt.)tractDiameters2`----------------------------------------
// Same with two independent constrictions, applied in order like the original's
// touch loop (each can only narrow what the previous ones left).
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// tractDiameters2(tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, c1i, c1d, c1a, c2i, c2d, c2a) : si.bus(44)
// ```
//
// Where:
//
// * `tongueIndex`: Tongue position in sections, 12..29 (default 12.9).
// * `tongueDiameter`: Tongue diameter in model units, 2.05..3.5 (default 2.43).
// * `c1i`: First constriction position in sections, 2..44.
// * `c1d`: First touch diameter in model units, 0..3; at most 0.3 closes the tract.
// * `c1a`: First constriction gate, 0 or 1.
// * `c2i`: Second constriction position in sections, 2..44.
// * `c2d`: Second touch diameter in model units, 0..3; at most 0.3 closes the tract.
// * `c2a`: Second constriction gate, 0 or 1.
//
// #### Test
// ```
// import("stdfaust.lib");
// tractDiameters2_test = pt.tractDiameters2(20, 3.0, 36.3, 0.5, 1, 20.6, 0.8, 1);
// ```
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
declare tractDiameters2 license "MIT";
tractDiameters2(tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, c1i, c1d, c1a, c2i, c2d, c2a) =
    par(i, _n, _moveTowards(_slowReturn(i)*_movementSpeed, 2*_movementSpeed, target(i)))
with {
    target(i) = _constrictedDiameter(c2i, c2d, c2a, i,
                _constrictedDiameter(c1i, c1d, c1a, i,
                                    _restDiameter(tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, i)));
};

// Fixed nose diameters (Tract.init); section 0 is the velum, replaced dynamically.
_noseDiameterInit(i) = min(1.9, ba.if(d < 1, 0.4 + 1.6*d, 0.5 + 1.5*(2 - d)))
with { d = 2*(i/_noseLength); };

// Nose reflections are computed once at init in the original with noseA[0]=0.16.
_noseArea(i) = _noseDiameterInit(i)*_noseDiameterInit(i);
_noseReflection(i) = (_noseArea(i-1) - _noseArea(i))/(_noseArea(i-1) + _noseArea(i));

//=========================== Tract waveguide ==========================================
//======================================================================================

_NSTATE = 2*_n + 2*_noseLength;  // 144 state signals: R[0..43], L[0..43], NR[0..27], NL[0..27]
_NREFL = _n - 1 + 3;            // reflection coefficients: refl[1..43], reflLeft, reflRight, reflNose


// Compile-time conditional for route() positions (c must be a constant 0/1).
_cif(c, a, b) = c*a + (1-c)*b;

// One waveguide tick (the original's Tract.runStep): state, glottal, inj[0..43],
// reflections -> state.
_tractTick = addInjections : junctionRoute : junctions : reorder : damping
with {
    // ---- stage A: R[k] += inj[k], L[k] += inj[k]; pass the rest through ----
    NIN = _NSTATE + 1 + _n + _NREFL;
    NA = 4*_n + 2*_noseLength + 1 + _NREFL;
    addInjections = route(NIN, NA,
                          par(k, _n, (k+1, 2*k+1), (_NSTATE+2+k, 2*k+2)),             // R[k], inj[k]
                          par(k, _n, (_n+k+1, 2*_n+2*k+1), (_NSTATE+2+k, 2*_n+2*k+2)),   // L[k], inj[k]
                          par(k, 2*_noseLength, (2*_n+k+1, 4*_n+k+1)),                 // NR, NL
                          (_NSTATE+1, 4*_n+2*_noseLength+1),                           // glottal
                          par(k, _NREFL, (_NSTATE+1+_n+k+1, 4*_n+2*_noseLength+1+k+1)))  // reflections
                  : par(k, _n, +), par(k, _n, +), si.bus(2*_noseLength), _, si.bus(_NREFL);

    // ---- stage B: scattering junctions ----
    // Input order after stage A (1-based): R'[k]=k+1, L'[k]=n+k+1, NR[k]=2n+k+1,
    // NL[k]=2n+_noseLength+k+1, glottal, refl[1..43], reflLeft, reflRight, reflNose.
    inR(k) = k+1;
    inL(k) = _n+k+1;
    inNR(k) = 2*_n+k+1;
    inNL(k) = 2*_n+_noseLength+k+1;
    inG = _NSTATE+1;
    inRefl(i) = _NSTATE+1+i;              // i = 1..43
    inReflLeft = _NSTATE+1+_n;
    inReflRight = _NSTATE+2+_n;
    inReflNose = _NSTATE+3+_n;
    // Block input offsets (number of inputs consumed before each block):
    // glottalEnd(2), junction(1..16)(3 each), noseJunction(6), junction(18..43)(3 each),
    // lipEnd(1), noseJunction(1..27)(2 each), noseEnd(1).
    offR(i) = _cif(i <= _noseStart, 3*i-1, 3*i+2);        // i >= 1
    offLipL = 3*_n+2;                                    // 134
    offNJ(i) = offLipL+1 + 2*(i-1);                     // i >= 1
    offNoseL = offLipL+1 + 2*(_noseLength-1);            // 189
    NB = offNoseL+1;                                    // 190 = inputs consumed by stage B
    junctionRoute = route(_NSTATE+1+_NREFL, NB,
        (inL(0), 1), (inG, 2),                                        // glottal end
        par(j, _n-1, jr(j+1)),                                         // interior junctions
        (inR(_n-1), offLipL+1),                                        // lip end
        par(j, _noseLength-1, (inNR(j), offNJ(j+1)+1), (inNL(j+1), offNJ(j+1)+2)),
        (inNR(_noseLength-1), offNoseL+1))
    with {
        jr(17) = (inReflLeft, offR(17)+1), (inReflRight, offR(17)+2), (inReflNose, offR(17)+3),
                 (inR(16), offR(17)+4), (inL(17), offR(17)+5), (inNL(0), offR(17)+6);  // _noseStart
        jr(i)  = (inRefl(i), offR(i)+1), (inR(i-1), offR(i)+2), (inL(i), offR(i)+3);
    };
    // scattering blocks
    glottalEnd(l0, g) = l0*_glottalReflection + g;                     // -> jR[0]
    junction(r, a, b) = a - w, b + w with { w = r*(a + b); };         // (r, R[i-1], L[i]) -> (jR[i], jL[i])
    noseJunction(rl, rr, rn, a, b, c) =                               // (.., R[i-1], L[i], NL[0])
        rr*b + (1+rr)*(a + c),                                        // jR[i]
        rl*a + (1+rl)*(c + b),                                        // jL[i]
        rn*c + (1+rn)*(b + a);                                        // nJR[0]
    lipEnd = *(_lipReflection);
    blockR(0)  = glottalEnd;
    blockR(17) = noseJunction;                                        // _noseStart
    blockR(i)  = junction;
    junctions = par(i, _n, blockR(i)), lipEnd,
                par(j, _noseLength-1, junction(_noseReflection(j+1))), lipEnd;

    // ---- stage C: back to state order (R = 0.999*jR[k], L = 0.999*jL[k+1], ...) ----
    // Output positions (1-based) of stage B: glottalEnd(1), junction i (2 each),
    // noseJunction(3), lipEnd(1), nose junction i (2 each), noseEnd(1).
    posJR(0) = 1;
    posJR(k) = _cif(k <= _noseStart, 2*k, 2*k+1);
    posJL(k) = _cif(k <= _noseStart, 2*k+1, _cif(k == _n, 2*_n+1, 2*k+2));
    posNJR(0) = 2*_noseStart+2;                                        // 36
    posNJR(k) = 2*_n+2 + 2*(k-1);
    posNJL(k) = _cif(k == _noseLength, 2*_n + 2*_noseLength, 2*_n+2 + 2*(k-1) + 1);
    reorder = route(_NSTATE, _NSTATE,
        par(k, _n, (posJR(k), k+1)),
        par(k, _n, (posJL(k+1), _n+k+1)),
        par(k, _noseLength, (posNJR(k), 2*_n+k+1)),
        par(k, _noseLength, (posNJL(k+1), 2*_n+_noseLength+k+1)));
    damping = par(k, 2*_n, *(_tractDamping)), par(k, 2*_noseLength, *(_noseDamping));
};

// Scattering coefficients from the 44 section diameters and the velum diameter
// (outputs ordered like _NREFL).
_tractReflections = route(_n+1, 2*(_n-1) + 3,
                         par(i, _n-1, (i+1, 2*i+1), (i+2, 2*i+2)),     // (d[i-1], d[i]) pairs
                         (_noseStart+1, 2*(_n-1)+1), (_noseStart+2, 2*(_n-1)+2), (_n+1, 2*(_n-1)+3))
                 : par(i, _n-1, refl), noseJunctionRefl
with {
    refl(d0, d1) = select2(a1 == 0, (a0 - a1)/max(ma.EPSILON, a0 + a1), 0.999)
    with { a0 = d0*d0; a1 = d1*d1; };
    noseJunctionRefl(d0, d1, dv) = (2*a0 - sA)/sA, (2*a1 - sA)/sA, (2*av - sA)/sA
    with { a0 = d0*d0; a1 = d1*d1; av = dv*dv; sA = a0 + a1 + av; };
};

//------------------------`(pt.)tract`----------------------------------------
// The Pink Trombone vocal tract: 44-section Kelly–Lochbaum waveguide with a
// 28-section nasal branch, ticked twice per sample. Diameters, constriction and
// velum drive the reflection coefficients; fricative noise and closure-release
// transients are injected into the waveguide.
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// tract(tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, cIndex, cDiameter, cActive, nasal, glottalOutput, noiseModulator) : _
// ```
//
// Where:
//
// * `tongueIndex`: Tongue position in sections, 12..29 (default 12.9).
// * `tongueDiameter`: Tongue diameter in model units, 2.05..3.5 (default 2.43).
// * `cIndex`: Constriction position in sections, 2..44; position 44 lies beyond the mouth cells.
// * `cDiameter`: Touch diameter in model units, 0..3; at most 0.3 closes the tract, 3 leaves it open.
// * `cActive`: Constriction gate, 0 or 1.
// * `nasal`: Velum gate: positive selects diameter 0.4; zero selects 0.01.
// * `glottalOutput`: Audio excitation from glottis or an external source.
// * `noiseModulator`: Turbulence amplitude modulator, normally the second output of glottis.
//
// #### Test
// ```
// import("stdfaust.lib");
// tract_test = (os.lf_imptrain(140), 0.3) : pt.tract(12.9, 2.43, 30, 3, 0, 0);
// tract_nasal_test = (os.lf_imptrain(140), 0.3) : pt.tract(27, 2.2, 30, 3, 0, 1);
// tract_closure_test = (os.lf_imptrain(140), 0.3) : pt.tract(12.9, 2.43, 40, 0, 1, 0);
// tract_release_test = (os.lf_imptrain(140), 0.3) : pt.tract(12.9, 2.43, 30, 0, ba.time < 12000, 0);
// ```
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
declare tract license "MIT";
tract(tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, cIndex, cDiameter, cActive, nasal, glottalOutput, noiseModulator) =
    tractExt(_fricativeNoise, tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, cIndex, cDiameter, cActive, nasal, glottalOutput, noiseModulator);

//------------------------`(pt.)tract2`----------------------------------------
// `tract` with two independent constrictions (the original is multi-touch: each
// touch narrows the tract and injects its own turbulence). Useful for consonant
// clusters and double articulations.
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// tract2(tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, c1i, c1d, c1a, c2i, c2d, c2a, nasal, glottalOutput, noiseModulator) : _
// ```
//
// Where:
//
// * `tongueIndex`: Tongue position in sections, 12..29 (default 12.9).
// * `tongueDiameter`: Tongue diameter in model units, 2.05..3.5 (default 2.43).
// * `c1i`: First constriction position in sections, 2..44.
// * `c1d`: First touch diameter in model units, 0..3; at most 0.3 closes the tract.
// * `c1a`: First constriction gate, 0 or 1.
// * `c2i`: Second constriction position in sections, 2..44.
// * `c2d`: Second touch diameter in model units, 0..3; at most 0.3 closes the tract.
// * `c2a`: Second constriction gate, 0 or 1.
// * `nasal`: Velum gate: positive selects diameter 0.4; zero selects 0.01.
// * `glottalOutput`: Audio excitation from glottis or an external source.
// * `noiseModulator`: Turbulence amplitude modulator, normally the second output of glottis.
//
// #### Test
// ```
// import("stdfaust.lib");
// tract2_test = (os.lf_imptrain(140), 0.3) : pt.tract2(12.9, 2.43, 36.3, 0.5, 1, 20.6, 0.8, 1, 0);
// ```
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
declare tract2 license "MIT";
tract2(tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, c1i, c1d, c1a, c2i, c2d, c2a, nasal, glottalOutput, noiseModulator) =
    tract2Ext(_fricativeNoise, tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, c1i, c1d, c1a, c2i, c2d, c2a, nasal, glottalOutput, noiseModulator);

//------------------------`(pt.)tractExt`----------------------------------------
// Same as `tract` / `tract2` but with an explicit turbulence noise source (the
// original's 1 kHz, Q 0.5 bandpassed white noise) as first argument, for testing.
//
// With `fricNoise = 0` and *constant* articulation arguments, `tractExt`/`tract2Ext`
// reduce to the bare linear waveguide, which is exactly LTI from `glottalOutput`
// to the output: `_moveTowards` starts on its target, so constant articulation
// never ramps, the reflection coefficients are constants, and no release
// transient can fire. Its impulse response then characterises it completely
// (useful for FIR/formant analysis of a fixed vocal-tract shape).
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// tractExt(fricNoise, tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, cIndex, cDiameter, cActive, nasal, glottalOutput, noiseModulator) : _
// ```
//
// Where:
//
// * `fricNoise`: External turbulence signal, typically white noise bandpassed at 1 kHz with Q 0.5; zero disables turbulence.
// * `tongueIndex`: Tongue position in sections, 12..29 (default 12.9).
// * `tongueDiameter`: Tongue diameter in model units, 2.05..3.5 (default 2.43).
// * `cIndex`: Constriction position in sections, 2..44; position 44 lies beyond the mouth cells.
// * `cDiameter`: Touch diameter in model units, 0..3; at most 0.3 closes the tract, 3 leaves it open.
// * `cActive`: Constriction gate, 0 or 1.
// * `nasal`: Velum gate: positive selects diameter 0.4; zero selects 0.01.
// * `glottalOutput`: Audio excitation from glottis or an external source.
// * `noiseModulator`: Turbulence amplitude modulator, normally the second output of glottis.
//
// #### Test
// ```
// import("stdfaust.lib");
// tractExt_test = pt.tractExt(no.noise, 12.9, 2.43, 30.4, 0.55, 1, 0, os.lf_imptrain(140), 0.3);
// ```
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
declare tractExt license "MIT";
tractExt(fricNoise, tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, cIndex, cDiameter, cActive, nasal, glottalOutput, noiseModulator) =
    tract2Ext(fricNoise, tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, cIndex, cDiameter, cActive, 30, 3, 0, nasal, glottalOutput, noiseModulator);

//------------------------`(pt.)tract2Ext`----------------------------------------
// Vocal tract with two independent constrictions and an explicit turbulence source.
// With zero turbulence and constant articulation, this is a linear time-invariant
// filter of the glottal excitation. Constant articulation starts on its target.
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// tract2Ext(fricNoise, tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, c1i, c1d, c1a, c2i, c2d, c2a, nasal, glottalOutput, noiseModulator) : _
// ```
//
// Where:
//
// * `fricNoise`: External turbulence signal, typically white noise bandpassed at 1 kHz with Q 0.5; zero disables turbulence.
// * `tongueIndex`: Tongue position in sections, 12..29 (default 12.9).
// * `tongueDiameter`: Tongue diameter in model units, 2.05..3.5 (default 2.43).
// * `c1i`: First constriction position in sections, 2..44.
// * `c1d`: First touch diameter in model units, 0..3; at most 0.3 closes the tract.
// * `c1a`: First constriction gate, 0 or 1.
// * `c2i`: Second constriction position in sections, 2..44.
// * `c2d`: Second touch diameter in model units, 0..3; at most 0.3 closes the tract.
// * `c2a`: Second constriction gate, 0 or 1.
// * `nasal`: Velum gate: positive selects diameter 0.4; zero selects 0.01.
// * `glottalOutput`: Audio excitation from glottis or an external source.
// * `noiseModulator`: Turbulence amplitude modulator, normally the second output of glottis.
//
// #### Test
// ```
// import("stdfaust.lib");
// tract2Ext_test = pt.tract2Ext(no.noise, 12.9, 2.43, 36.3, 0.5, 1, 20.6, 0.8, 1, 0, os.lf_imptrain(140), 0.3);
// ```
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
declare tract2Ext license "MIT";
tract2Ext(fricNoise, tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, c1i, c1d, c1a, c2i, c2d, c2a, nasal, glottalOutput, noiseModulator) =
    excBus : (body(ticksPerSample) ~ par(k, _NSTATE, _flush)) : (par(k, _NSTATE, !), _) : *(0.25/ticksPerSample)
with {
    NTRB = 2*2 + 3*2;       // (transEnv, transPos) per transient slot, then (turb, idx, delta) per constriction
    NEXC = 1 + _n + _NREFL;   // glottal, inj[0..43], reflections

    // ---- geometry (each signal generator instantiated ONCE; multiply-used buses
    //      are distributed with explicit fan-out `<:` so the *box* graph stays small —
    //      Faust substitutes `with`-definitions textually, and letting each of the 44
    //      injection taps close over the diameter graph made the block diagram
    //      explode: the WASM compiler of the online IDE ran out of memory
    //      generating the SVG) ----
    velumTarget = select2(nasal > 0, 0.01, 0.4);
    velum = _moveTowards(0.25*_movementSpeed, 0.1*_movementSpeed, velumTarget);
    diameters = tractDiameters2(tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, c1i, c1d, c1a, c2i, c2d, c2a);

    // ---- turbulence noise level at each constriction ----
    // The original also skips a touch with `diameter <= 0`, but that guard is
    // subsumed by `openness` (already 0 for cd <= 0.3), so only the index
    // bounds are kept here.
    turbOf(ci, cd, ca) = 0.66*fricNoise*fricIntensity*noiseModulator*thinness*openness
                       * (ci >= 2) * (ci <= _n)
    with {
        fricIntensity = _moveTowards(10, 10, ca > 0) : aa.clip(0, 1);  // 0.1 s attack/release
        thinness = 8*(0.7 - cd) : aa.clip(0, 1);
        openness = 30*(cd - 0.3) : aa.clip(0, 1);
    };
    turbBus = turbOf(c1i, c1d, c1a), floor(c1i), c1i - floor(c1i),
              turbOf(c2i, c2d, c2a), floor(c2i), c2i - floor(c2i);

    // ---- transients: (lastObstruction, velum) -> (transEnv, transPos) ----
    // The original detects the release in `reshapeTract`, one block after the
    // diameter first became positive, so the pulse is delayed by one block here too.
    obstructedIdx(i, d) = ba.if(d <= 0, i, -1);
    lastObsAndVelum = (par(i, _n, obstructedIdx(i)) : ba.parallelMax(_n)), _;  // d[0..43], velum -> lastObs, velum
    transientPair(lo, vel) = env(1), pos(1), env(0), pos(0)
    with {
        blockSamples = int(512*2/ticksPerSample);   // one original block
        releaseTrig = (((lo' > -1) & (lo == -1) & (1')) @ blockSamples) & (vel*vel < 0.05);
        // two slots, used alternately, so an earlier transient keeps sounding at
        // its own position when a new one is released
        slot = ((+(releaseTrig)) ~ _) % 2;
        env(j) = (\(e).(e*pow(2, -200.0/ma.SR) + 0.3*releaseTrig*(slot == j))) ~ _;  // strength 0.3, exponent 200
        pos(j) = _latch(releaseTrig*(slot == j), lo' @ blockSamples);
    };

    // one injection tap: (transEnv, transPos, (turb, idx, delta)x2) -> inj[k]
    injTap(k) = \(e, p, eb, pb, t1, ix1, dl1, t2, ix2, dl2).(
        0.5*e*(k == p) + 0.5*eb*(k == pb)
      + 0.5*t1*((k == ix1+1)*(1 - dl1) + (k == ix1+2)*dl1)
      + 0.5*t2*((k == ix2+1)*(1 - dl2) + (k == ix2+2)*dl2));

    // ---- the excitation bus: glottal, inj[0..43], reflections (built once) ----
    excBus = glottalOutput,
             (((diameters, velum) <: (_tractReflections, lastObsAndVelum))  // refl(_NREFL), lastObs, velum
              : (si.bus(_NREFL), transientPair), turbBus                    // refl(_NREFL), e, p, eb, pb, turbBus(6)
              : route(_NREFL+NTRB, _NREFL+NTRB,
                      par(i, _NREFL, (i+1, i+NTRB+1)),
                      par(i, NTRB, (_NREFL+1+i, i+1)))                      // e, p, turbBus(6), refl(_NREFL)
              : (si.bus(NTRB) <: par(k, _n, injTap(k))), si.bus(_NREFL));    // inj(n), refl(_NREFL)

    // ---- ticksPerSample waveguide ticks per sample, summing lip+nose output of each ----
    tapOut = si.bus(_NSTATE) <: si.bus(_NSTATE), (route(_NSTATE, 2, (_n, 1), (2*_n + _noseLength, 2)) : +);  // lipOutput + noseOutput
    tickTap = _tractTick : tapOut;                                          // state, exc -> state, out
    // body: state, exc -> state, summed output of each tick (exc duplicated as
    // wires, not as subgraphs). Two ticks per sample (the original) or one.
    body(1) = tickTap;
    body(2) = (si.bus(_NSTATE), (si.bus(NEXC) <: si.bus(2*NEXC)))
         : (tickTap, si.bus(NEXC))
         : route(_NSTATE+1+NEXC, _NSTATE+NEXC+1,
                 par(i, _NSTATE, (i+1, i+1)),
                 (_NSTATE+1, _NSTATE+NEXC+1),
                 par(i, NEXC, (_NSTATE+2+i, _NSTATE+1+i)))
         : (tickTap, _)
         : (si.bus(_NSTATE), +);
    // state below 1e-20 is flushed to zero (the lossless nose would otherwise
    // decay into denormals)
    _flush(x) = select2(abs(x) < 1e-20, x, 0.0);
};

//=========================== Full instrument ==========================================
//======================================================================================

//------------------------`(pt.)pinkTrombone`----------------------------------------
// Glottis + tract. Mono output.
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// pinkTrombone(freq, tenseness, voiced, wobble, tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, cIndex, cDiameter, cActive, nasal) : _
// ```
//
// Where:
//
// * `freq`: Positive fundamental frequency in Hz; the demo spans about 87..277 Hz.
// * `tenseness`: Voice tenseness in 0..1; the default is 0.6.
// * `voiced`: Voice gate: positive is on, zero is off. It acts like a finger on the
//   original's pitch keyboard: voicing ramps in and out, with no pressed onset.
// * `wobble`: Pitch wobble amount in 0..1.
// * `tongueIndex`: Tongue position in sections, 12..29 (default 12.9).
// * `tongueDiameter`: Tongue diameter in model units, 2.05..3.5 (default 2.43).
// * `cIndex`: Constriction position in sections, 2..44; position 44 lies beyond the mouth cells.
// * `cDiameter`: Touch diameter in model units, 0..3; at most 0.3 closes the tract, 3 leaves it open.
// * `cActive`: Constriction gate, 0 or 1.
// * `nasal`: Velum gate: positive selects diameter 0.4; zero selects 0.01.
//
// #### Test
// ```
// import("stdfaust.lib");
// pinkTrombone_test = pt.pinkTrombone(140, 0.6, 1, 0, 12.9, 2.43, 30, 3, 0, 0);
// ```
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
declare pinkTrombone license "MIT";
pinkTrombone(freq, tenseness, voiced, wobble, tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, cIndex, cDiameter, cActive, nasal) =
    pinkTrombone2(freq, tenseness, voiced, wobble, tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, cIndex, cDiameter, cActive, 30, 3, 0, nasal);

//------------------------`(pt.)pinkTrombone2`----------------------------------------
// Glottis + tract with two constrictions. Mono output.
//
// #### Usage
//
// ```
// pinkTrombone2(freq, tenseness, voiced, wobble, tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, c1i, c1d, c1a, c2i, c2d, c2a, nasal) : _
// ```
//
// Where:
//
// * `freq`: Positive fundamental frequency in Hz; the demo spans about 87..277 Hz.
// * `tenseness`: Voice tenseness in 0..1; the default is 0.6.
// * `voiced`: Voice gate: positive is on, zero is off. It acts like a finger on the
//   original's pitch keyboard: voicing ramps in and out, with no pressed onset.
// * `wobble`: Pitch wobble amount in 0..1.
// * `tongueIndex`: Tongue position in sections, 12..29 (default 12.9).
// * `tongueDiameter`: Tongue diameter in model units, 2.05..3.5 (default 2.43).
// * `c1i`: First constriction position in sections, 2..44.
// * `c1d`: First touch diameter in model units, 0..3; at most 0.3 closes the tract.
// * `c1a`: First constriction gate, 0 or 1.
// * `c2i`: Second constriction position in sections, 2..44.
// * `c2d`: Second touch diameter in model units, 0..3; at most 0.3 closes the tract.
// * `c2a`: Second constriction gate, 0 or 1.
// * `nasal`: Velum gate: positive selects diameter 0.4; zero selects 0.01.
//
// #### Test
// ```
// import("stdfaust.lib");
// pinkTrombone2_test = pt.pinkTrombone2(140, 0.6, 1, 0, 12.9, 2.43, 40, 0.2, 1, 20, 1.0, 1, 1);
// ```
//-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
declare pinkTrombone2 license "MIT";
pinkTrombone2(freq, tenseness, voiced, wobble, tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, c1i, c1d, c1a, c2i, c2d, c2a, nasal) =
    glottis(freq, tenseness, voiced, wobble) : (_,_,!,!)
    : tract2(tongueIndex, tongueDiameter, c1i, c1d, c1a, c2i, c2d, c2a, nasal);
